<title>USA: FP&amp;L Turkey Pt 4 returns to full power.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L Turkey Pt 4 returns to full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power and Light Co's 666 megawatt (MW) Turkey Point 4 nuclear power unit has resumed full operations, Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Wednesday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, in Florida City, Fla., was operating at 60 percent power Tuesday for condenser waterbox cleaning and other maintenance.</p>
<p>The adjacent 666 MW unit, Turkey Point 3, is still operating at 100 percent of capacity.</p>
<p>Florida Power is a subsidiary of the FPL Group.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
